From 7414087ae227e9a99bdf9004acfb669eaf2b54ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:00:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/97] xam: fix dangling root name in deferred
 XamContentCreate; log content API calls

The deferred XamContentCreate lambda captured root_name.value() - a string_view
into guest memory - and read it later on the dispatch thread. WWE '13 reuses that
stack buffer, so its DLC packages were mounted under a garbage root ('pB?p:') and
dlc0:\info\catalog.dlc could not resolve (the game reported the DLC as corrupted).
The root name is now copied at call time. Audit of the other deferred Xam
handlers: XamShowKeyboardUI now copies default_text before scheduling. Content API
calls and stub exports are logged at info level (no behaviour change).

WWE '13 title update + DLC Packs 2/3: both packs mount as dlc0:/dlc1: with the
installed license, catalogs and DLC_02/03.pck open; 900 s run 0 captures, in-ring
criterion met.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
